WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.738
Step six drafts the findings: six
to open, two to close, no comments.

2
00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.312
Then search the drafts.

3
00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:12.950
For a user's address, grep counts zero;
the name isn't there, and grep exits one.

4
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.425
For the object ID, it counts one.

5
00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:19.675
The tracker gets the object ID and
the fingerprint, never the name.

6
00:00:19.675 --> 00:00:21.858
Step seven packages the second day,

7
00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:26.300
chained to the first with the previous
manifest option, and verifies it.

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:32.275
The manifest hash starts oh nine three
two, and verify reports sixteen files.

9
00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:36.348
Then the ISSO's own check,
with no program code at all:

10
00:00:36.348 --> 00:00:42.263
sha two fifty-six sum, in the package's
folder, prints nothing and exits zero.

11
00:00:42.263 --> 00:00:48.440
Last, read two fields of day two's manifest:
the previous package's manifest hash,

12
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:53.951
which is day one's, six d nine f f f,
and the fixture tenant's placeholder ID.

13
00:00:53.951 --> 00:00:55.060
That's the chain.
